# Build output and downloaded dependencies.
#
# Makina asks agents to build and verify their work, then commits the whole
# task worktree. Anything a build writes that is not ignored here is committed
# with the task and rejected as outside its authored footprint — so these rules
# are what keep the first task that compiles anything from failing the run.
#
# Add your own; nothing below is removed by Makina.

# Rust
/target/

# JavaScript / TypeScript
node_modules/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# OS noise
.DS_Store

# What a long run writes beside itself when it is started with `nohup`: the
# six-hour soak the release checklist asks for is started that way, and its
# console output belongs with the run's own artifacts, not in the tree.
/nohup.out

# Makina runtime state, when it is kept inside the checkout.
/.worktrees/

# Agent and editor state never belongs to the repository; the rules that
# apply here live in AGENTS.md, and tooling configuration lives at user level.
/.claude/
/CLAUDE.md
